// The scheduler: the behaviours that `when` schedules, run by worker threads. No behaviour runs natively yet, so the
// entry stub's calls find nothing to do.

// schedDrain is what the entry stub calls after main: it runs behaviours until none is left, and gives back main's exit
// code.
function schedDrain(code Count) returns Count
	return code
end 'schedDrain'

// workerMain is what a thread the runtime makes runs, with its context, which rt.threadStart has stored in the
// thread-local slot.
function workerMain(context Count)
	return
end 'workerMain'
